<%# Fuime: what the OPERATOR is agreeing to, said to the operator.

    The seller-of-record framing was already reasoned about carefully in this
    codebase — and every word of it was in ERB comments and admin screens. A
    teenager publishing an offer was told the price was theirs and nothing else:
    not that Fuime is the legal seller, not that a customer can refund within 14
    days, not that a refund comes off what they are owed, not that a chargeback is
    Fuime's to answer. They found out when a number moved.

    Two reasons this has to be visible rather than filed in the terms:

    1. It is their money. A refund debit on `Fuime::PayablesLedger` that arrives
       unexplained reads as Fuime taking their earnings.
    2. It is the contractor characterisation (MOR_RISK_ACCEPTANCE.md §2 Q2). "You
       set your prices, you choose your customers, Fuime never assigns work" is the
       fact that keeps an operator a vendor rather than an employee — and a fact
       nobody has been told is a fact nobody can rely on.

    Deliberately plain language and short sentences. The audience is 13.

    Merchant-of-record only: under Connect the guardian's own account is the
    merchant, the guardian carries the chargeback, and all of this would be wrong. %>
<% if ::Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
  <div class="card bg-snow mt-4">
    <h2 class="mt0 mb-2 text-lg">How selling through Fuime works</h2>
    <ul class="mb-2" style="line-height: 1.6;">
      <li>
        <strong>You set your own price.</strong> Nobody at Fuime sets it, suggests
        it, or tells you which customers to take. That is yours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fuime LLC is the legal seller.</strong> Your customer buys from
        Fuime, Fuime appears on their card statement, and Fuime pays you for the
        work as its vendor. You are not Fuime's employee.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Customers can ask for a refund within 14 days.</strong> Fuime
        handles it and pays it back to them — you never have to argue with a
        customer about money.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A refund comes off what Fuime owes you</strong> for that sale. You
        will see it on your earnings as "Refunds and disputes", so a drop is never
        a mystery.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>If a customer disputes a charge with their bank, that is Fuime's
        to answer, not yours.</strong>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Payment problems go to
        <a href="mailto:support@fuime.com">support@fuime.com</a></strong> — not to
        you. Send anyone who asks straight to us.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted text-sm mb-0">
      The full version is in the <%= link_to "terms", terms_path %>, section 8.
    </p>
  </div>
<% end %>
